# Separate finance contexts
# caption: What it settles. What CIC bills a client and what a client bills a homeowner are different ledgers with different payers, even when they share a payment provider. Twilio minutes are a usage measurement that passes through the existing reviewer gate, never a direct invoice line.
flowchart TB
    Usage["Operator One usage and contract"] --> Bill["Client BillingAccount and Invoice"]
    Job["Client field-service work"] --> Field["End Customer FieldInvoice"]
    Bill --> Corp["Corporate ledger and merchant context"]
    Field --> Client["Client ledger and merchant context"]
    Corp --> Adapter["Scoped payment and accounting adapters"]
    Client --> Adapter
    Adapter --> Rail["Payment rail"]
    Adapter --> Books["Accounting ledger"]
  